Evidence A - boot log of a crashing pod (release 2026.10.26-2):
[Nest] 1  - 10/26/2026, 9:31:42 AM     LOG [NestFactory] Starting Nest application...
[Nest] 1  - 10/26/2026, 9:31:42 AM   ERROR [ExceptionHandler] Nest cannot create the EnrollmentModule instance.
The module at index [0] of the EnrollmentModule "imports" array is undefined.

Potential causes:
- A circular dependency between modules. Use forwardRef() to avoid it. Read more: https://docs.nestjs.com/fundamentals/circular-dependency
- The module at index [0] is of type "undefined". Check your import statements and the type of the module.

Scope [AppModule -> CourseModule]

Evidence B - PR #731 "enrollments: block enrolling before prerequisites are completed", enrollment.module.ts:
 import { Module } from "@nestjs/common";
+import { CourseModule } from "../courses/course.module";
 import { EnrollmentRepository } from "./enrollment.repository";
 import { EnrollmentService } from "./enrollment.service";

 @Module({
+  imports: [CourseModule],
   providers: [EnrollmentRepository, EnrollmentService],
   exports: [EnrollmentService],
 })
 export class EnrollmentModule {}
(app.module.ts imports CourseModule first; course.module.ts has imported EnrollmentModule since PR #702.)

Statement: "The undefined entry at index [0] is CourseModule: enrollment.module.ts ran while course.module.ts was still loading, because the two files import each other."

Proposed fix:
// enrollments/enrollment-data.module.ts (new)
@Module({ providers: [EnrollmentRepository], exports: [EnrollmentRepository] })
export class EnrollmentDataModule {}

// courses/course.module.ts - CourseService now injects EnrollmentRepository and calls countByCourse()
@Module({ imports: [EnrollmentDataModule], providers: [CourseRepository, CourseService], exports: [CourseService] })
export class CourseModule {}

// enrollments/enrollment.module.ts - EnrollmentService injects EnrollmentRepository and CourseService
@Module({ imports: [CourseModule, EnrollmentDataModule], providers: [EnrollmentService], exports: [EnrollmentService] })
export class EnrollmentModule {}

// app.module.ts (unchanged)
@Module({ imports: [CourseModule, EnrollmentModule] })
export class AppModule {}

Statement: "With this change the module import graph has no cycle, and CourseService and EnrollmentService receive the same EnrollmentRepository instance."
